# Repo-wide EOL policy. Text files normalize to LF in the index; the
# working tree gets LF on checkout regardless of host OS (Windows, mac,
# Linux). Windows-native script formats keep CRLF because their runtimes
# choke on bare LF (PowerShell, cmd.exe shim, .bat).
#
# Binary detection is `text=auto`: git inspects content and skips files
# that look binary (e.g. plugins/mccp/scripts/receipt/dedupe.js, which
# contains an intentional `\0` separator). That auto-detection is fine —
# do not promote `*.js text` blanket because it would break dedupe.js.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1 eol=crlf
*.cmd eol=crlf
*.bat eol=crlf
